/**
 * GATE 10 on DuckDB (//core:stress_suites): the stress corpus's service suites ({@link StressSuites}) on one seeded
 * session per distinct provisioning, shared across the tests that declare it (isolation by write detection: a session
 * that executed a statement with an effect is re-seeded before the next test). The count judged EQUAL to the referee may
 * only grow: raise {@link #MIN_PASS} with every leg that burns a bucket; never lower it. The measuring knobs (data
 * overrides, row dumps, one service, a session policy) are {@code bazel run //core:stress_tool}'s (Bazel workplan
 * P3-12).
 */
@org.junit.jupiter.api.Tag("stress")   // GATE 10: its own gate, excluded from the core suite by tag
@DisplayName("Stress corpus: service test suites through legend-lite (DuckDB)")
class StressServiceSuitesTest {

    /** Tests judged equal to the referee (first full run 2026-09-16: 2,702 of 4,736). Shrink-proof. */
    static final int MIN_PASS = 5519;   // 5479 -> 5519 (2026-10-30, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 5: M2M chained over relational sources; the 40 relational twins over the m2m:: source model pass; every M2M service lite loads, 34 MX_ with M1_TradeCanonical and M2_CanonicalWithEnum (55-canonical-chain.pure, out of the measure's exclusion), runs and fails on one lite gap, the test runtime losing the ModelChainConnection's mapping (`has 0 mappings binding class`), and the merge as an implicit union; the enumeration transforms and the passthrough are in 8115-m2m-gaps.pure, which lite excludes (the user's choice), with their services; spread.py's one changed selection passes as the one it replaced did; the count rose by exactly the 40 twins) 5453 -> 5479 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 7 stage 3: the unused joins mapped, 26 of 31 passing, UJ_JoinArrayArg among them (the engine's is F83); the others are a runtime holding two mappings that bind one class (class-query dispatch needs exactly one: UJ_ClassificationCounterparty, UJ_CounterpartyClassification, UJ_CounterpartyOtcTrades) and a join's != and <> over a NULL, which lite reads as Pure's not(equal(...)) and so matches, where the store's SQL matches nothing (UJ_JoinNotEqual, UJ_JoinAnsiNotEqual); of the 142 services whose expectations moved with the deleted joins, each that passed still passes; no test that passed fails) 5445 -> 5453 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 7 stage 2: the Operation forms moved into 71-operation-surface.pure, 8 of 12 passing: the router union and the inheritance dispatch, each projected and fetched, and the store's two joins as a chain, and ending in an expression; the others are a literal list over an optional column (`Collection element must have a multiplicity [1]`) and the merge operation, a class mapped by several sets, whose .all() lite reads as an unsupported implicit union; no test that passed fails) 5325 -> 5445 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 7 stage 1: the 60 classes stress::DenseMapping maps, each projected through the flat mapping and through DenseMapping, 120 of 120 passing; no test that passed fails) 5324 -> 5325 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md: F37's property-mapping half withdrawn by the user (a mapping's substring is the relational dynafunction, SQL's): F37_SubstringSql now asserts 'lpha' and passes; the combination matrix's 12 new substring cells pass once RelOpTranslator wraps the substring dynafunction's operands in toOne, as its generic dyna path does (a column reached through a join had failed to type against Pure's strict substring, sinking CB_C7, CB_C9, CB_C10 and SP_ComboC9Group); no test that passed fails) 5291 -> 5324 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 4 stage 6: the last PCT names, 33 of 49 passing, VR_Lag2 among them (lite's lag honours its offset; the engine's is F80); the others are TV-04's trimmed trailing space (toUpperFirstCharacter, toLowerFirstCharacter, regexpReplace, splitPart, the let column), map over an absent value (F68's shape: between, greatest, least) and sum over no trades as NULL (F82's shape); no test that passed fails) 5264 -> 5291 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md: the plan's D8 reversed by the user: a groupBy aggregate over a group whose values are all absent is absent, its count 0, as legend-engine's groupBy native and its PCT define it; F75 withdrawn, and the 24 deep-stack totals and VGN_SumQuantity, VGN_SumRate and VGN_SumAmount, which lite answers NULL, pass again; VGN_JoinStringsName still meets TV-04's trimmed trailing space; no test that passed fails) 5213 -> 5264 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 4 stage 5: the remaining scalars and control flow, 51 of 64 passing; the others are bitShiftLeft of a negative number (F78's shape), parseDecimal cast to DECIMAL(5,2), TV-04's trimmed trailing space (left, right, jaroWinklerSimilarity), and asin and acos through map over an absent value answering true (F68's shape); no test that passed fails) 5178 -> 5213 (2026-10-29, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 4 stage 4: relation and TDS shapes, 35 of 40 passing; the others are substring(start) read one-based in an extend, both paradigms, and olapGroupBy's ranking func (a bare lambda has no type outside a call position); no test that passed fails) 5135 -> 5178 (2026-10-28, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 4 stage 3: the aggregates in a groupBy, 67 of 77 passing; the others are F75's and F76's shapes (lite answers SQL's NULL over an all-absent group and the sample variance of one value, as the engine does), TV-04's trimmed trailing space in joinStrings, `last` (no row scope for $agg) and wavgRowMapper (an unknown function); 24 deep-stack grouped totals that passed now fail, their expectation moved from null to legend-pure's 0 (F75); no other test that passed fails) 4939 -> 5135 (2026-10-28, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 4 stage 2: the function vocabulary, 196 of 258 passing; the others are TV-04's trimmed trailing space (Phase 1's bucket), 32-bit overflow (F71's shape), indexOf as strpos (F72's) and map over an absent value (F68's); no test that passed fails) 4869 -> 4939 (2026-10-28, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 3: the intraday milestoning services, 70 of 90 passing; the 20 others take parameters, Phase 1's bucket; no test that passed fails) 4849 -> 4869 (2026-10-27, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 2: the seed spines and the deep variants re-rooted at classes with rows; 527 passing tests left the corpus, 547 came in and pass, and no test that passed fails) 4839 -> 4849 (2026-10-23, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 1: ten more enumeration-literal services, each value under `!=` and `||` of two, all passing) 4705 -> 4839 (2026-10-23, docs/STRESS_CORPUS_PLAN_2026_10_19.md Phase 1: the typed-value services, 133 of them passing, and CB_NotEqualsNull, whose expectation now reads `!=` over an absent value as legend-pure does; F28 withdrawn) 4700 -> 4705 (2026-10-05: the referee's dateDiff follows legend-pure's elapsed time, F58; five services agree) 2702 -> 2765 -> 4203 -> 4564 -> 4626 -> 4654 -> 4672 -> 4679 -> 4689 (2-ULP judge policy F-AE; 2026-09-16/17: double division; pins; association anchors; F-M; F-O; orElse → coalesce; OR/range navigation aggregates; timestamp JSON spelling; isAlphaNumeric + firstHourOfDay on DuckDB + splitPart index base; view column kinds + grouped-predicate scoping + routed sub-join key demand)


    @Test
    void suites() throws Exception {
        assertAtLeast(TestBackends.platform(), MIN_PASS);
    }

    /** One full run on {@code backend}, its pass count at or above {@code floor}. */
    static void assertAtLeast(TestBackend backend, int floor) throws Exception {
        StressSuites.Result r = StressSuites.run(new StressSuites.Config(backend, null, "", List.of(), null, com.legend.testing.TestOutputs.dir()));
        assertFalse(r.pass().isEmpty(), "nothing passed — the harness itself is broken");
        assertTrue(r.pass().size() >= floor, r.pass().size() + " tests passed, below the ratchet " + floor
                + " — see stress-suites-fail*.txt in the test's outputs");
    }
}
